 say help.zig stays attributed to jnagpaul and Dhole. It lists Wen Li at 40 lines in args.zig, which is not the required claim.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives a bus factor of 3, which is a fail condition.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A says 668 lines (43.5%) would have no author left and cites 79% belonging to inactive people. It does not give the combined ~85% figure, and its numbers are muddled (24% active, 79% inactive).\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A does not clearly name jnagpaul, Vincent and mochalins as having left. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives Felix 36% of all lines because Wen Li's generated table is counted. It gives 46% excluding the table, but its headline is 36%, which is below the 43% lower bound.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives Wen Li 26% (4% without the table), above the 2.5% limit, and does not say help.zig stays attributed to its original authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives a bus factor of 2, but it is built from Felix plus Wen Li instead of Felix plus jnagpaul. It does say jnagpaul's last commit was in 2023, and it gives Felix at 46% without the table, needing a second person. Arguably it meets the second branch, but its headline Felix figure of 36% is off and the pairing is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives only Felix's own 36% or 46% as the loss. It mentions inactive authors at 37% separately but does not combine them into about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B names jnagpaul (2023), Vincent Rischmann (2025) and mochalins (2025) as quiet. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion, and its 90-day window treats Felix as not recently active.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives Felix 37% of all lines including the generated table, and about 48% without it. The headline figure is below 43%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives Wen Li 25%, mostly the generated table, and says that table is generated data. It does not give Wen Li's hand-written share as 2.5% or less, and it does not attribute help.zig to jnagpaul and Dhole.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives a bus factor of about 2 using Felix and Wen, not jnagpaul, and does not say jnagpaul stopped contributing.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives only Felix's 37% as the loss, with no combined figure with already-departed authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C does not list who has left and does not credit Dmitri Volkov.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Felix 39% of lines, below the 43% lower bound.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D says help.zig is 100% Tobias Ek, which is a stated fail condition.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives a bus factor of 4 (the tool reports 6), which is 3 or more and fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives only Felix's 39% as the loss. It does say 9 of 13 files are mostly inactive, but gives no combined figure of about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D treats Felix as inactive, which is a fail condition, and does not name the departed authors.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Felix about 37% (831 of 2,225), below the 43% lower bound.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Wen Li 25% and does not say help.zig stays attributed to its original authors. It does say Tobias Ek has only 5 lines, which is a minor point.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E says the bus factor is about 2 for the repo, but it uses Felix plus Wen Li and does not mention jnagpaul stopping. Its Felix share of 37% is also off.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives only Felix's 37% as the loss and says no part of the code is fully orphaned, which contradicts the ground truth.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E does not list departed authors and does not credit Dmitri Volkov.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives Felix 35.8% of lines, below the 40% fail threshold.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives Wen Li 26%, and it recommends that Tobias Ek review the code. It does not say help.zig stays attributed to jnagpaul and Dhole.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives a bus factor of 2, but it uses Felix plus Wen Li and says Felix is already inactive. It does not mention jnagpaul stopping.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives only Felix's 36% as the loss, with no combined figure of about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F describes Felix as no longer active (no commits in 90 days), which is a fail condition.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":13811,"type":"result","duration_ms":13838,"uuid":"a522ec87-87a2-49d7-8f78-7db54ebd7d0f","ttft_stream_ms":2017,"time_to_request_ms":649,"first_content_frame_ms":2017,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
